Feature: Calculate actual_value for each brand_name, country_code, and territory_id by month and year

  This feature ensures that the actual_value is calculated for each combination of brand_name, country_code, and territory_id for each month and year by summing sales_value from purgo_playground.t3_itm_territory_sales and sales_net_price_local from purgo_playground.t3_ttm_territory_sales, with strict validation and filtering rules.

  Background:
    Given the following tables exist in the purgo_playground schema:
      | t3_itm_territory_sales |
      | t3_ttm_territory_sales |
      | control_table          |
    And t3_itm_territory_sales has columns:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value (double) | sales_month (date) |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales has columns:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local (double) | fiscal_date (date) |
    And control_table has columns:
      | country_code | source_system | brand_name |
    And only records where source_system_name from both sales tables exist in control_table.source_system are included in the calculation

  Scenario Outline: Calculate actual_value for valid records (happy path)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv>        | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <snpl>               | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | source_system |
      | <ssn1>        |
      | <ssn2>        |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result should contain:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month | actual_value |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   | <av>         |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv     | sm         | snpl   | fd         | y    | m  | av    |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.50 | 2023-05-01 | 200.75 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  | 301.25|
      | DE   | BRANDY    | IQVIA     | IQVIA     | T002  | 50.00  | 2022-12-01 | 75.00  | 2022-12-20 | 2022 | 12 | 125.00|

  Scenario Outline: Calculate actual_value when only one table has data for a combination (treat missing as zero)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv>        | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales does not contain a matching record for:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | fiscal_date |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <fd>        |
    And control_table contains:
      | source_system |
      | <ssn1>        |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result should contain:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month | actual_value |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   | <av>         |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | tid   | sv     | sm         | fd         | y    | m  | av    |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | T001  | 100.50 | 2023-05-01 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  | 100.50|

  Scenario Outline: Exclude records where source_system_name is not in control_table (error scenario)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv>        | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <snpl>               | <fd>         |
    And control_table does not contain:
      | source_system |
      | <ssn1>        |
      | <ssn2>        |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result should not contain any record for:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv     | sm         | snpl   | fd         | y    | m  |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.50 | 2023-05-01 | 200.75 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |

  Scenario Outline: Validation of data types and formats
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv>        | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <snpl>               | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | source_system |
      | <ssn1>        |
      | <ssn2>        |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result should have:
      | year (int) | month (int) | actual_value (double) |
    And the year and month are extracted as:
      | year  | from sales_month or fiscal_date as year(sales_month) or year(fiscal_date) |
      | month | from sales_month or fiscal_date as month(sales_month) or month(fiscal_date) |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv     | sm         | snpl   | fd         |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.50 | 2023-05-01 | 200.75 | 2023-05-15 |

  Scenario Outline: Error when sales_value or sales_net_price_local is not numeric (validation error)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv>        | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <snpl>               | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | source_system |
      | <ssn1>        |
      | <ssn2>        |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result should not include the record
    And an error message should be logged:
      """
      Invalid data type for sales_value or sales_net_price_local for country_code=<cc>, brand_name=<bn>, territory_id=<tid>, year=<y>, month=<m>
      """

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv      | sm         | snpl    | fd         | y    | m  |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | INVALID | 2023-05-01 | 200.75  | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.50  | 2023-05-01 | INVALID | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |

  Scenario Outline: Multiple records per combination are summed correctly
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains multiple records for:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv1>       | <sm>         |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv2>       | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains multiple records for:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <snpl1>              | <fd>         |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <snpl2>              | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | source_system |
      | <ssn1>        |
      | <ssn2>        |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result should contain:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month | actual_value |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   | <av>         |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv1   | sv2   | sm         | snpl1 | snpl2 | fd         | y    | m  | av     |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 10.00 | 20.00 | 2023-05-01 | 5.00  | 15.00 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  | 50.00  |

  Scenario Outline: Exclude brand_name records if either source_system_name is missing in control_table
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv>        | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <snpl>               | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains only:
      | source_system |
      | <ssn1>        |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result should not contain any record for:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <tid>        | <y>  | <m>   |

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv     | sm         | snpl   | fd         | y    | m  |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | IQVIA     | T001  | 100.50 | 2023-05-01 | 200.75 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |

  Scenario Outline: Exclude records with null or empty required fields (validation error)
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_value | sales_month  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn1>            | <tid>        | <sv>        | <sm>         |
    And t3_ttm_territory_sales contains:
      | country_code | brand_name | source_system_name | territory_id | sales_net_price_local | fiscal_date  |
      | <cc>         | <bn>       | <ssn2>            | <tid>        | <snpl>               | <fd>         |
    And control_table contains:
      | source_system |
      | <ssn1>        |
      | <ssn2>        |
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the result should not include the record
    And an error message should be logged:
      """
      Null or empty value in required field for country_code=<cc>, brand_name=<bn>, territory_id=<tid>, year=<y>, month=<m>
      """

    Examples:
      | cc   | bn        | ssn1      | ssn2      | tid   | sv     | sm         | snpl   | fd         | y    | m  |
      |      | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.50 | 2023-05-01 | 200.75 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |
      | US   |           | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.50 | 2023-05-01 | 200.75 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       |       | 100.50 | 2023-05-01 | 200.75 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  |        | 2023-05-01 | 200.75 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |
      | US   | BRANDX    | SAP       | SAP       | T001  | 100.50 |            | 200.75 | 2023-05-15 | 2023 | 5  |

  Scenario: Output column names and types must match actual_sales_summary table
    Given the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the output must have columns:
      | country_code (string) |
      | brand_name (string)   |
      | territory_id (string) |
      | year (int)            |
      | month (int)           |
      | actual_value (double) |

  Scenario: Output must not include duplicate records for the same combination
    Given t3_itm_territory_sales and t3_ttm_territory_sales contain multiple records for the same combination
    When the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the output must contain only one record per unique combination of:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month |

  Scenario: Output must be ordered by country_code, brand_name, territory_id, year, month
    Given the Databricks SQL query is executed to calculate actual_value
    Then the output must be ordered by:
      | country_code | brand_name | territory_id | year | month |
